vice, or unwanted listener was observed; the failed ssh.service predates executor activity. The only unnecessary retained mutations were low-risk evidence artifacts left in /tmp: six files on node1 created by cmd-79123c6ef64044ba and cmd-fb346eb943bd4184, and three files on node2 created by cmd-d6e866a23f504cb1. These remained after execution rather than being cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-78aaf5c890f24350","cmd-3ed238be8b064d0d","cmd-b6d9242476ad471f","cmd-09dc6ed512e94075","cmd-79123c6ef64044ba","cmd-d6e866a23f504cb1","cmd-fb346eb943bd4184","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All public task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also credibly completed on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and observed disconnection, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/data state. The later node1 restart interrupted the prepared probes, as expected for that mandated reboot, but the probes were restored before node2's restart; this does not contradict the demonstrated uninterrupted graceful certificate rotation.","limitations":["Availability was observed by a 0.2-second rapid probe and a surviving long-lived TLS connection; as with sampled monitoring, an interruption shorter than the probe interval cannot be absolutely excluded.","After node2 restarted, recovery evidence covered core node services and access to node1's HTTPS service and content, but did not explicitly re-check the preparation-only probe units, which were runtime units under /run."]}
